  {
    "sha": "768f64a308a8c1c10994622369c65d4716eff794",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDc2OGY2NGEzMDhhOGMxYzEwOTk0NjIyMzY5YzY1ZDQ3MTZlZmY3OTQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T00:56:24Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-13T00:56:24Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(project): load pre-v59 meshes as \"fidelity unknown\" and refuse them by name until re-imported\n\nA project saved before #911 recorded no mesh fidelity, so a STEP model\nits import kept coarser than promised loaded as full fidelity with no\nre-check. Re-measuring on load is impossible (the chord is measured\nagainst the B-rep; the file keeps only facets), and a v58 file cannot\ntell a pre-#911 save from a later fine one, nor STEP from STL.\n\n- PROJECT_VERSION 59. Loading an older file marks every mesh without a\n  recorded chord (models, fixtures, from-model stock copies) \"fidelity\n  unknown\", with one load note each (project::fidelity_migrate). A\n  recorded coarse_mm is kept.\n- The mark is the sentinel chord model_fidelity::UNKNOWN_MM on the\n  existing ReducedFidelity component, so it rides every copy, clone,\n  undo and save path the flag rides. The gate refuses every operation\n  judged against it by name, an unknown part refuses the program verdict,\n  an unknown fixture refuses through its own gate line; the sim and the\n  eye judge nothing. Model page / MCP / script say \"Fidelity unknown\".\n- Saved as \"fidelity_unknown\": true (never a chord number); both keys on\n  one row is corrupt. Only a fresh import clears it.\n- examples/first-part and the microARC kit project (exact OBJ / code\n  meshes) re-stamped v59.\n\nDecision in docs/decisions/1056-fidelity-unknown.md.\n\nFixes #1056\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
      "tree": {
